        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add channel field to ADSEXTERNALCONVERSIONPOSTBACKFIELDS",
        "summary": "Added `channel` to `ADS_EXTERNAL_CONVERSION_POSTBACK_FIELDS` in `common/src/util/axiom-only-log.ts` to distinguish between 's2s' (key-authenticated) and 'client' (keyless browser) ingress. This field is strictly two-valued and never carries partner identifiers, aligning with the requirement to keep Axiom logs bounded to operational dimensions. The change ensures correct telemetry routing and filtering without expanding the log schema into attribution records.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T04:14:44.057Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Internal logging now records whether a conversion came through a direct server call (labeled 's2s') or a browser-based request (labeled 'client'). This only affects how the company's own monitoring tools sort and filter incoming conversion reports, so engineers can better tell apart the two pathways. You as an outside observer won't see a visible change, it's a behind-the-scenes tweak to keep internal tracking organized.",
