        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add ADPLACEMENTCPCGEOFLOORCENTS constant",
        "summary": "Introduced `AD_PLACEMENT_CPC_GEO_FLOOR_CENTS` (50) in `common/src/constants/freebuff-topups.ts`. This sets the minimum billing price for a single geo-adjusted click after country multipliers apply. It remains distinct from `AD_PLACEMENT_CPC_FLOOR_CENTS`, which enforces the campaign's base rate floor. The separation ensures geo pricing requires no migration, as `ck_ad_placement_campaign_cpc_floor` continues guarding the base rate.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T04:14:20.207Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Advertisers now have a new minimum price that applies only to individual clicks from countries where they pay less per click. This is separate from their regular minimum rate, so when clicks from a low-cost country get scaled down, each one will bill for at least fifty cents rather than potentially rounding down to a lower amount. The change is already live in the system and applies automatically to the geo-adjusted pricing; no action is needed to turn it on.",
