        "summary": "A new dependency-free module `common/src/constants/agentic-ad-events.ts` defines the event vocabulary for sponsored proposals surfaced through the first-party placements rail, covering stages from `proposal_offered` through `tool_used`. Of these, only accepted is billable, and it settles as a CPC click through the existing first-party click path (`settleFirstPartyClick`) rather than via funnel-event recording; all other stages are telemetry for pricing the next campaign. A second subset, `AGENTIC_POSTBACK_EVENT_TYPES`, restricts which events an advertiser may report via the S2S postback (`POST /api/ads/agentic/postback`) to `account_created` and `tool_used`.",
